What is Lag in Time Series?

A Lag means using a previous value of the time series.

Simply:

Lag 1 (t-1) = Previous value
Lag 2 (t-2) = Value before previous value
Lag 3 (t-3) = Three steps back
Example from Your Image

| Date     | Value | Value(t-1) | Value(t-2) |
| -------- | ----: | ---------: | ---------: |
| 1/1/2017 |   200 |         NA |         NA |
| 1/2/2017 |   220 |        200 |         NA |
| 1/3/2017 |   215 |        220 |        200 |
| 1/4/2017 |   230 |        215 |        220 |
| 1/5/2017 |   235 |        230 |        215 |
| 1/6/2017 |   225 |        235 |        230 |

=======

Understanding Lag 1

For date 1/4/2017:

Current Value = 230

Lag 1 = Previous day's value

230 ← Current Value
215 ← Lag 1
Understanding Lag 2

For date 1/4/2017:

Current Value = 230

230 ← Current Value
215 ← Lag 1
220 ← Lag 2
